<Project Sdk="AsmFoundation.Sdk/ASMSDK_VERSION">
  <!--
    AsmWasm.1: a WebAssembly library written in assembly. "dotnet build" builds it for both
    WebAssembly runtimes on any build machine (the SDK brings llvm-mc and wasm-ld; nothing to
    install), under bin/<Configuration>/freestanding/<rid>/:
      AsmWasm.1.wasm   the module: JavaScript and WASI hosts instantiate it and call its exports
      AsmWasm.1.a      the archive: a .NET WebAssembly app (Blazor, wasmbrowser) links it
    add.wasm.s is the code, in LLVM's WebAssembly assembly. "node run.mjs" calls it.

    Call it from a .NET WebAssembly app (RuntimeIdentifier browser-wasm or wasi-wasm, with the
    wasm-tools workload): add <ProjectReference Include="../AsmWasm.1/AsmWasm.1.asmproj" /> to
    its .csproj, then declare each function on a static partial class:
      [LibraryImport("AsmWasm.1", EntryPoint = "add_ints")]
      internal static partial int AddInts(int a, int b);
    The "asmwasmapp" template sets such an app up for you.

    The SDK version is the one on the first line; change it there to upgrade.
    Documentation: https://asmfoundation.github.io/AsmSdk/guide/webassembly.html
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <RuntimeIdentifiers>browser-wasm;wasi-wasm</RuntimeIdentifiers>
  </PropertyGroup>
</Project>
